  "credit": "NASA's release and press kit, Spaceflight Now, collectSPACE, SpacePolicyOnline and Space.com for the launch, descent and loss of the mission; LROC (NASA/GSFC/Arizona State University) for the landing coordinates. Conflicts kept open: the main-engine relight is about 17:15 UTC (collectSPACE, converted) against 17:27 UTC (Wikipedia only); touchdown is about 17:30 UTC (NASA) or 17:28:50 UTC (Wikipedia); the distance from the target is 250 m (Intuitive Machines) or more than 400 m (NASA). Intuitive Machines says only that Athena hit the surface faster than intended; a figure of 10 to 13 m/s circulates in a page that could not be opened, is unverified and is not used. Tilt, IM-2's dry mass, main-engine thrust and Isp were not found. The wet mass is from Wikipedia only (IM-1: 2,035 kg in NASA's technical memorandum).",
